  "title": "Stomachache",
  "content_type": "paragraph",
  "content_text": "Stomachache\n[肚子疼]\nOn Sunday, I got up around noon again, just like yesterday.\n[周日，像昨天一样睡到大中午才起来。]\nWhile washing up, I felt a dull pain in my stomach and immediately thought of the culprit—the ginger duck I had last night.\n[洗漱的时候就感觉肚子隐隐作痛，一下子就联想到了罪魁祸首——昨晚吃的仔姜鸭。]\nGinger duck has been my favorite dish since I came to Chengdu, but it’s still too spicy for my stomach.\n[仔姜鸭是我来到成都后最喜欢的一道菜，但是它对于我的肠胃来说还是太辣了。]\nSometimes I’m fine after eating it, but other times—like today—it messes up my stomach.\n[有时吃没啥事，有时却会像今天一样闹肚子。]\nEvery time this happens, I swear I won’t eat it again, but I always give in to temptation.\n[每次闹肚子时候都会决心说下次不吃了，但是还是嘴馋。]\nThis time, I need to set a reasonable rule: no more than once a week, and preferably on a non-working day.\n[这次需要设定一个合理的要求，即一周最多吃一次，最好是非工作日吃。]",
  "created_at": "2025-11-08T18:32:17.787046Z",
